\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The H-standard. A representation is hierarchical when all five hold. Thresholds were fixed before any audit run. H1 and H2 are decided by the spectrum and the top-8 column: a gapless spectrum fails H1, and if the slowest-sorted dimensions carry no more slow content than random, H2 fails with them.}}{5}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:hstandard}{{1}{5}{The H-standard. A representation is hierarchical when all five hold. Thresholds were fixed before any audit run. H1 and H2 are decided by the spectrum and the top-8 column: a gapless spectrum fails H1, and if the slowest-sorted dimensions carry no more slow content than random, H2 fails with them}{table.1}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The audit. Five systems against the H-standard, measured on the same teleoperated PushT data (collected by the authors on a push-T task). The H-JEPA backbone enters the structural audit in Sec.~\ref {sec:handplaced}, where its spectrum is measured directly. H3a reports the top-8 slow-content recovery as a fraction of the full-128 recovery; the threshold is 0.8. The best system (LeWM) reaches 0.64; none passes. H4 shows the ratio $\epsilon ^* / \mathrm  {null}$ over $K = 2$ to 5 blocks; the threshold is 0.5. The LeWM $h^*$ entry comes from the macro-5 natural experiment (Sec.~\ref {sec:phenomenon}); its own stride-1 H5 was not measured. Every system fails every structural criterion.}}{5}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:audit}{{2}{5}{The audit. Five systems against the H-standard, measured on the same teleoperated PushT data (collected by the authors on a push-T task). The H-JEPA backbone enters the structural audit in Sec.~\ref {sec:handplaced}, where its spectrum is measured directly. H3a reports the top-8 slow-content recovery as a fraction of the full-128 recovery; the threshold is 0.8. The best system (LeWM) reaches 0.64; none passes. H4 shows the ratio $\epsilon ^* / \mathrm {null}$ over $K = 2$ to 5 blocks; the threshold is 0.5. The LeWM $h^*$ entry comes from the macro-5 natural experiment (Sec.~\ref {sec:phenomenon}); its own stride-1 H5 was not measured. Every system fails every structural criterion}{table.2}{}}
